            <div xml:id="d481">

                <pb facs="1052" n="956" sameAs="frus:frus1945Malta/pg956"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Defense Files: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-02-06">6 February
                        1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>To Secretary of State from Ambassador Winant London serial number 2072.</p>
                <p>Soviet acting representative on the European Advisory Commission has informed me
                    that his government has approved the Protocol on zones of occupation and the
                    control machinery agreement for Germany. All 3 governments have now approved
                    without reservation the 3 basic documents for the control of Germany—the
                    instrument of unconditional surrender, the Protocol on zones of occupation and
                    the agreement on control machinery.</p>
            </div>
